  Status: author draft; independent mathematical and source-correspondence
  review pending. Source revision inspected:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

  <section|Scope><label|scope>

  The prose is <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-freight-producer.tex>.
  It follows the public selected-run producer of the finite-volume transfer
  representation used by the centered estimate. Its central mathematical work
  is the finite backward construction of compatible voices and the algebraic
  normalization of the transfer frame. It proves the finite induction and its
  exact finite-sum integral identity from the selected one-step ticket
  estimates.

  The finite interpolation ticket is still a stated quantitative input here.
  The proof does not derive all local field interpolation and shipment prices
  from primitive resource data. This chapter is therefore a checked producer
  stage, not a claim that the complete public theorem has become
  unconditional.

  <section|Public route and source correspondence><label|public-route-and-source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Prose
  assertion>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned declarations /
  paths>>|<cell|<strong|Inspection note>>>|<row|<cell|Public run fixes one
  history and calls the producer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.ramp>,
  <verbatim|.Run.again>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Cross.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|ramp>
  chooses the purchased trajectory, obtains the nested history and calls
  <verbatim|Bandage.squad> once with a common grade-reference schedule. It
  stores the resulting transfer maps, makes, doors, climbs, and
  <verbatim|Freight> records on the same run. <verbatim|again> passes those
  records to <verbatim|ahead>.>>|<row|<cell|Backward music and freight
  definition>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.Freight>,
  <verbatim|.squad>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Marco.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Freight>
  is a selected music with terminal top voice, initial transfer entries equal
  to its draft, a paid <verbatim|Sung> bound, and a <verbatim|Carol> response
  plus <verbatim|Chorus> condition at every in-range adjacent scale.
  <verbatim|squad> proves this for all grades and finite-volume pairs at or
  beyond the chosen reference.>>|<row|<cell|Doors and selected finite
  interpolation ticket>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.chorus>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Cub.clocksHere>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.jewelCard>, <verbatim|.basalCard>,
  <verbatim|.heavyK>, <verbatim|.turnout>, and
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Cub.leading>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Escarp.lean>, <verbatim|Crowding.lean>,
  <verbatim|Rosin.lean>, <verbatim|Basal.lean>, <verbatim|Beacon.lean>,
  <verbatim|Volley.lean>, <verbatim|PhysicalNext/RG_NEXT_COMPLETE_REPEATABLE_NONLINEAR_STEP/Cub/Direction.lean>>|<cell|The
  held spring gives the gate and climb. At <verbatim|d+3\<leq\>J_m>,
  <verbatim|clocksHere> forms the stored flight matrix and cap, obtains the
  heading forecast from the selected schedule-price bound, and returns a
  single heading with <verbatim|Stampede> for any wing containing all origin
  principal modes. Its three certificate fields are proved separately: the
  principal-field estimate gives the axis coupon; the supported-field/regular
  estimate gives the regular coupon; the slot-fit/forced-field estimate gives
  the marked forced coupon. The forecast plus the cap's triangular-price
  bound gives both heading-map norm bounds. <verbatim|turnout> packages these
  into <verbatim|Stampede>. <verbatim|chorus> applies this output to the
  finite union of origin modes and terminal-keeper sites. The source waybill
  is <verbatim|2 exp(fine supportExponent) * profileTitle>; the exact prices
  are <verbatim|C=E(J_m)> for residuals and <verbatim|w=Doors.rate(block_m)>
  for lead coefficients, and the forced divisor is the square root of the
  forced allowance. The source's selected <verbatim|Chop>,
  <verbatim|Doors.Budget>, slot, arrival/rate, and keeper packages remain
  explicit hypotheses of this construction; this unit does not derive those
  packages from the lower resource purchases.>>|<row|<cell|Top voice and
  reflection condition>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.summon>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Inception.voice>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Calling.lean> (summon dependencies) and
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Inception.lean>>|<cell|The terminal keeper is
  the one attached to the nested birth data. The selected trajectory's
  terminal representation and receipt give the top readout identities; the
  sound section and real/selected history give the reflection condition.
  <verbatim|voice> proves terminal <verbatim|Chorus> from <verbatim|OnTop>,
  reality, and the exact motion pull identity.>>|<row|<cell|Finite endpoint
  response>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Matric.repriseQ>,
  <verbatim|.motor>, <verbatim|.sends>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Renaissance.lean>,
  <verbatim|Vega.lean>, <verbatim|Wheels.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|repriseQ>
  first applies the single-coordinate ticket to each axis coefficient. With
  <math|s> paid columns and ticket amounts <math|C,\<eta\>,t>, the exact
  enlarged values are <math|c=C+\<eta\>*s>,
  <math|\<epsilon\>=\<eta\>*<around|(|1+s|)>>, and <math|t+2*s>. It applies
  every signed motion, assembles the finite tally with the frame's
  <verbatim|chips> coefficients, and uses
  <verbatim|pencil>/<verbatim|pencil_ledger> to obtain linearity, the pushed
  density identity, the forced-profile sum, and the charged wing bound.
  <verbatim|motor> proves the endpoint estimate by integral push,
  interpolation, audition, and remnant bounds. The prose displays the finite
  sum and exact transition-integral interchange; the paid column
  interpolation inequalities are kept as inputs from the
  ticket.>>|<row|<cell|Finite backward induction>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Matric.composeT>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.compose>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Mark/Vega.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Largo.lean>>|<cell|Both source recursions
  initialize a zero-padded music with the supplied terminal voice, apply the
  one-step response at the next lower index, and update only that music
  coordinate. The update formula leaves all strictly later voices unchanged,
  so previously obtained <verbatim|Sung>, <verbatim|Carol>, and
  <verbatim|Chorus> conditions persist. The prose spells out this finite
  induction rather than treating a trajectory as a limiting
  object.>>|<row|<cell|Initial transfer normalization>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.G08.answer>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/G08.lean>>|<cell|The source defines the transfer
  entries from the recursively built voices. Its reference map is injective:
  a zero at the reference propagates through the finite cone recurrence to a
  zero at the terminal frame, where the readout is an isomorphism. Finite
  dimensionality then makes the map bijective, and its inverse supplies the
  normalized frame. <verbatim|G08.answer> fills the reference,
  forward/backward, linear, real, orientation, and paid cone fields of the
  transfer structure. The prose explains the finite-dimensional injectivity
  argument and the role of each identity.>>|<row|<cell|Assembly into
  <verbatim|Makes> and exact Freight>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.squad>;
  <verbatim|YM.Source.Family.normalized>,
  <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Issue.refer>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Marco.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Source/Construction.lean>, and
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/SOURCE_HISTORIES/Issue.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|squad>
  applies <verbatim|Issue.refer> to construct the family-level
  support/stage/fit and loading facts, then takes the exact
  <verbatim|Freight> witness for each grade/volume/period. Out-of-range
  transfer entries are padded trivially and never used by the claimed
  range.>>|<row|<cell|Same-history receipt into the centered
  supplier>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.nectar>,
  <verbatim|.hearthstone>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Gist.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Hearth.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|nectar> receives
  the <verbatim|Freight> family from the selected run and packages its Music,
  transition tales, and terminal forced-profile hook as the public
  <verbatim|Geyser> receipt. <verbatim|hearthstone> combines this with the
  selected one-scale prices and mark portfolios. It does not choose another
  history.>>|<row|<cell|Finite-volume expectation
  integrability>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.occurs>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Glacier.lean>>|<cell|The terminal product is
  continuous on compact configuration space and therefore integrable.
  <verbatim|occurs> propagates the birth polynomial by the normalized push
  recurrence and uses the Music/transfer coefficient identities at each
  scale. The centered chapter uses only finite integration and
  finite-dimensional coefficient extraction.>>>>>

  <section|Mathematical compression and limits><label|mathematical-compression-and-limits>

  The ordinary-math proof uses no infinite diagonal or compactness argument
  in this producer step. It uses finite sums over the source tally
  <verbatim|Motion \<times\> Index>, linearity and motion covariance of the
  normalized push, and finite downward induction on the scale interval. In
  the one-step assembly, the tally coefficients obey the exact frame identity
  <verbatim|v = sum_j chi(v,j) alpha_j>; the pushed density identity is
  obtained by applying the transition to this finite sum. The bounds on the
  absolute coefficient weights are exactly the paid ticket,
  frame-interpolation, and orbit-cost inequalities recorded in the selected
  history.

  The finite interpolation coupons are produced in the selected history by
  the clock/heading construction described above, from its principal-field,
  regular-field, and forced-slot estimates. The public route also constructs
  the door, terminal voice, and transfer/music package on the same history.
  This unit still assumes the selected schedule-price and budget certificate,
  the held spring with its endpoint fields, the arrival/rate and slot
  packages, the terminal keeper, and the terminal birth receipt. It does not
  derive those upstream packages from the original resource purchase. The
  centered bound is therefore conditional on these precisely named producer
  inputs.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Inspected only the exact route declarations and immediate producer
    dependencies listed above; no Lean files were changed and no Lean build
    was run.

    <item>No literature citation is applicable: this is a project-specific
    finite transfer and ticket construction, not a new analytic-limit
    theorem.

    <item>A temporary wrapper at <verbatim|/tmp/ym-centered-fragment.tex>
    includes the parent local-transfer chapter, centered extraction chapter,
    lattice chapter, <verbatim|centered-construction.tex>, this file, and
    <verbatim|centered-birth-receipt.tex>. <verbatim|latexmk -pdf
    -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error
    -outdir=/tmp/ym-centered-fragment-build /tmp/ym-centered-fragment.tex>
    succeeded after the current edits and produced a 36-page PDF. Eleven
    reference uses remain unresolved because the wrapper omits OPE, lattice
    rate/step, and column-subpower sections; no reference in this file is
    unresolved. One overfull box is in the lattice chapter, not in the
    centered chapters. Pages 27\U36 were rendered and inspected for layout.
    No Lean build or test was run.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run and fails
    because the shared, parent-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>
    is absent in this worktree. I did not create or alter that file.
  </itemize-minus>

